# Anthropological Mission {2}{U}: Enchantment
#   Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, put a quest counter on this enchantment. Draw a card. Then discard a card unless this enchantment has three or more quest counters on it.
# The Mission takes two quest counters on turn 1. On turn 3 the third Zuran Orb triggers it, and Bot2 returns it to
# Bot1's hand with Echoing Truth in response. Bot2 casts the bounce, not Bot1, because a spell Bot1 cast would trigger
# the Mission again, and that trigger would resolve first and add the third counter. The trigger then resolves with its
# source gone: no counter can be put on an object that changed zones (CR 400.7), so the condition reads the counters the
# Mission last had on the battlefield, two (CR 608.2h). Bot1 still draws, then discards. A counter put on the departed
# Mission would make three and skip the discard, leaving three cards in hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Anthropological Mission
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Zuran Orb
Zuran Orb
Zuran Orb
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Echoing Truth
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Anthropological Mission.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Zuran Orb.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Island)
Bot1.Hand.Zuran Orb.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Island)
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Anthropological Mission.Counters.Quest = 2
Bot1.Hand.Zuran Orb.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Echoing Truth.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Anthropological Mission)
Bot1.Choose(Island)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Zuran Orb; Zuran Orb; Zuran Orb
Bot1.Hand = Island; Anthropological Mission
Bot1.Graveyard = Island; Island; Island
Bot2.Graveyard = Echoing Truth
